---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What insulation should I use in a sauna?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Use the insulation and complete wall assembly specified by the approved sauna design, product instructions, local code, and building professional. The answer changes for a built-in room, freestanding panel room, detached outdoor structure, or room against a cold exterior wall.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What R-value does a sauna need?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'There is no universal R-value for every sauna and climate. Finnleo currently advises a minimum of R12 for walls and R16 for ceilings in its custom-sauna construction guidance, but another system, climate, or code may require a different assembly.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Does a sauna need a foil vapor barrier?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Many current Finnleo custom systems include a foil vapor barrier, but the correct air, vapor, and moisture-control layers depend on the complete assembly. Follow the sauna system, building design, climate, and local requirements rather than adding layers from a generic detail.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What should be planned before sauna paneling?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Harvia advises planning backing for wall-mounted heaters and benches and routing for the heater, controls, sensors, and lighting before paneling. Coordinate those items with insulation, air and vapor control, and inspection hold points before closing the wall.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Sauna Insulation Guide: Plan the Complete Wall Assembly"
  description="Plan sauna insulation, air and vapor control, backing, and wall sequencing by construction type. Compare current Finnleo, TyloHelo, and Harvia guidance."
  canonical="/guides/sauna-insulation"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Heat and moisture planning</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-3">Sauna Insulation: Plan the Complete Assembly</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500">Reviewed August 2026 &middot; Planning guide, not a construction detail</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mt-4">Insulation is only one layer. The enclosure must coordinate structure, heat, air, vapor, bulk water, drying, utilities, backing, and interior paneling as one system.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/sauna-interior-window.jpg" alt="Finished sauna interior whose concealed wall assembly must follow an approved project design" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="eager" width="1200" height="800" />
    </div>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Do not build from a generic layer list:</strong> A built-in indoor room, freestanding panel room, detached outdoor sauna, and room against a cold exterior wall can require different assemblies. Use the approved plans, sauna-system instructions, local code, climate, and qualified building professionals for the actual detail.
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-construction-type">
      <h2 id="insulation-construction-type" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">First identify the construction type</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {[
          ['Built-in indoor room', 'The sauna finish is installed inside framed walls. Coordinate the sauna enclosure with the home wall, ceiling, electrical, and mechanical assemblies.'],
          ['Freestanding panel room', 'The manufacturer supplies much of the enclosure. Preserve required clearances and do not block provided vents or service access.'],
          ['Detached outdoor structure', 'The hot-room assembly must also coordinate weather protection, drainage, structure, foundation, and the exterior climate.'],
          ['Room against an exterior wall', 'Cold-side conditions can change condensation and drying risk. TyloHelo describes a ventilated gap in its room-in-room example; another approved system may differ.'],
        ].map(([title, body]) => (
          <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="manufacturer-assembly-examples">
      <h2 id="manufacturer-assembly-examples" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">What current manufacturer guidance can establish</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-stone-200 rounded-lg">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[680px] text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-stone-900 text-white">
              <th class="text-left p-3">Source</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3">Published guidance</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3">How to use it</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-stone-700">
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border-b border-stone-200">Finnleo custom-sauna guidance</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Minimum R12 walls and R16 ceiling; its custom kits include foil vapor barrier.</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Treat these as Finnleo system guidance, not a universal code minimum.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-stone-50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border-b border-stone-200">TyloHelo room-in-room guide</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">A ventilated gap of about 20 mm is shown where the sauna adjoins an existing cold exterior wall.</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Use the complete TyloHelo detail only where it fits the approved project.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold">Harvia paneling guidance</td>
              <td class="p-3">Backing for wall heaters and benches and routes for heater, control, sensor, and lighting wiring must be planned before paneling.</td>
              <td class="p-3">Coordinate concealed support and utilities before insulation and finishes hide them.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="sauna_insulation_after_system_examples"
      heading="Put the wall assembly in the full project context"
      description="Capture the location, construction type, heater, dimensions, utilities, and installation needs before requesting a system-specific detail."
    />

    <section class="mt-10 mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-planning-sequence">
      <h2 id="insulation-planning-sequence" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">A safer planning sequence</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-4 text-stone-700 list-decimal pl-5">
        <li><strong>Define the boundaries.</strong> Mark which walls and ceilings adjoin interior conditioned space, exterior conditions, another wet area, attic space, or the outdoors.</li>
        <li><strong>Select the complete sauna system.</strong> Record the room or kit manufacturer, heater, controls, ventilation method, and all required manuals.</li>
        <li><strong>Get an assembly detail.</strong> The detail should show structure, insulation, air and vapor control, drainage, drying path, interior finish, and exterior weather layers where applicable.</li>
        <li><strong>Coordinate concealed work.</strong> Include backing for benches and wall equipment, electrical and sensor routes, lighting, vents, doors, and any required penetrations.</li>
        <li><strong>Set inspection hold points.</strong> Verify rough framing, moisture-control layers, utilities, and required inspections before paneling closes the assembly.</li>
        <li><strong>Document the finished work.</strong> Keep progress photos, approved substitutions, product data, permits, inspection records, and manuals.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-questions-for-designer">
      <h2 id="insulation-questions-for-designer" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Questions the detail should answer</h2>
      <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5">
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
          <li>[ ] Which insulation product and thickness belongs in each surface?</li>
          <li>[ ] Where are the air and vapor-control layers, and how are seams and penetrations handled?</li>
          <li>[ ] Does any existing exterior wall require a ventilated gap?</li>
          <li>[ ] How does the floor manage water, drainage, and drying?</li>
          <li>[ ] Where are heater, bench, guard, and accessory backing locations?</li>
          <li>[ ] How are wiring, sensors, lighting, and vents coordinated?</li>
          <li>[ ] Which concealed conditions require inspection before closure?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-mistakes">
      <h2 id="insulation-mistakes" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Mistakes to avoid</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          ['Copying one manufacturer detail into another system', 'A layer order or vent path that works in one complete design may conflict with another heater, room, or building assembly.'],
          ['Choosing R-value without checking the surface', 'Walls, ceilings, exterior boundaries, and outdoor structures do not face the same conditions.'],
          ['Adding a second vapor-control layer by instinct', 'Extra low-permeance layers can change drying. Have the complete assembly reviewed instead of combining isolated tips.'],
          ['Closing the wall before coordination', 'Missing backing, wiring, sensors, vents, or inspections creates expensive rework and can compromise the approved detail.'],
          ['Treating interior paneling as waterproofing', 'Wood paneling is a finish. Moisture, drainage, and drying must be handled by the complete assembly.'],
        ].map(([title, body]) => (
          <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 bg-white">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-sources">
      <h2 id="insulation-sources" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Primary sources used</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="https://www.finnleo.com/sauna-construction" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Finnleo sauna construction</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Current insulation, room-size, and ventilation planning guidance for Finnleo custom systems.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.tylohelo.com/hubfs/How%20to/Guide%20-%20How%20to%20build%20a%20sauna.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">TyloHelo build guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Room-in-room construction, insulation, air-gap, and paneling examples.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://support.harvia.com/hc/en-gb/articles/21953077934620-I-am-about-to-start-panelling-my-sauna-what-do-I-need-to-take-into-account" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400 md:col-span-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Harvia pre-paneling guidance</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Backing and concealed wiring decisions that must be made before paneling.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="insulation-faq">
      <h2 id="insulation-faq" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">What insulation should I use?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Use the product and thickness in the approved assembly. Do not choose insulation separately from the building, moisture, heater, and finish design.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Is R30 always required at the ceiling?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">No universal value applies. Finnleo currently publishes R16 as its minimum ceiling guidance for custom saunas, while climate, code, and another system may require something else.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Can I install paneling as soon as insulation is in?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Only after the required backing, utilities, control layers, product instructions, and inspections are complete and documented.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Continue the build plan</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-to-build-a-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Safe sauna build sequence</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-ventilation/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Ventilation by heater and airflow method</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-electrical-requirements/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Electrical planning guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-wood/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Sauna wood and material schedule</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
